    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T1OROUTC6",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: carry-out of stage 1, copy 6 of 7: same majority(A1, B1, C1) as T1OROUT, feeding T2H2N5C3.A. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_8eafe530f4224d358163dd533dc78ee0",
        "IdGuid": "269def99-3a61-4c22-aa0e-59cfd168d780",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "ba9643df-41e3-4ce4-86ab-2f65df206b9b",
          "efa048ee-f3ef-481c-a7dd-b9def16db350",
          "e067ad5d-2c48-46a3-82d9-b3fec5902128",
