    {
      "GroupDto": {
        "GroupName": "T2H1N1A5",
        "Description": "NAND reading (inputs A and B, BIAS constantly on, threshold 0.125) of the shipped \u0027Logic Gate NOT-NAND\u0027 gate. Role in the 4-bit adder: first XOR stage of stage 2\u0027s partial sum (chain 5 of 7), Y = NAND(A2, B2), feeding T2H1N25.B. The whole 4-bit adder composes at the logic layer, not optically: every gate\u0027s truth table is extracted once in isolation, so each stage restores clean 0/1 levels by construction \u2014 there is deliberately no multi-stage passive optical cascade here. The fan-out of the A, B and Cin bits onto several gates happens at the logic layer (each gate input is driven by the same network bit); shared stages \u2014 and each stage\u0027s carry-out, which must reach the next stage\u0027s several carry-in pins \u2014 are duplicated as extra gate instances because the canvas wires one waveguide per pin (like NAND1A/NAND1B in \u0027Logic Gate Half Adder\u0027).",
        "Identifier": "group_8847089957b0477cb8bfee58aabd840f",
        "IdGuid": "3e57114a-f3c4-4de6-b0cb-4d42f44b0f07",
        "ChildComponentGuids": [
          "fd44f3c9-0ef6-482c-bfa5-19f240e18223",
